# Review of the leak scanner, its exceptions and the workflows (2026-10-29).
# The box's agents act on GitHub as the account that opens every PR, and GitHub never asks
# an author to review their own PR, so this review comes from a separate person through
# this team. The allowlist approval label trusts only that person's numeric id (repository
# variable AE_LEAK_ALLOWLIST_APPROVERS, changed 2026-10-29). There is no catch-all line: a
# code-owner ruleset would then need an owner review on every PR, which the box account can
# never give. A ruleset requiring code-owner review and the leaks check follows once this
# merges.
/.github/workflows/ @analyticendeavors/leak-approvers
/.github/CODEOWNERS @analyticendeavors/leak-approvers
/scripts/leak-scan.py @analyticendeavors/leak-approvers
/scripts/leak-allowlist.txt @analyticendeavors/leak-approvers
/scripts/leak-fork-baseline.txt @analyticendeavors/leak-approvers
